# Byte fidelity is a correctness requirement in this project, not a preference.
#
# The .adk puzzle corpus is CRLF and 22 of the 96 files have no trailing newline.
# Field 3 of a record ("X" for X-sudoku) is followed by CR, and the Dart parser must
# split on /\r?\n/ to match the Java original. The global git config here sets
# core.autocrlf=input, which silently rewrites CRLF to LF on `git add` -- measured to
# strip all 718 CR bytes from squiggly_x_1.adk. That would make the port diverge from
# the Java oracle with no error anywhere. So: git performs NO line-ending conversion
# in this repository, for any file.
* -text

# Golden traces and digests are compared byte-for-byte.
*.zst   binary
*.trace binary
*.adk   binary
